      ],
      "text": "Legal ablations use idling: P2 alone releases only B1-B3; P1 alone cannot unload all nine source carriers without inspections freeing rack space. Broken-link idling collapses to a parent-alone control. Separate active disconnected co-presence is unavailable because P1 unloads onto the shared rack. Additional storage or bypass controls cannot be invented."
    },
    {
      "id": "R07-residue-defeat",
      "source_refs": [
