        "P2",
        "C3",
        "C5",
        "C6",
        "M3",
        "R2",
        "R3"
      ],
      "text": "Parent-only trip arithmetic already predicts the comparative transfer burden, defeating an interaction-specific explanation. Material dependence alone does not establish beneficial migration. Vehicle selection is allowed within P1, but changed duration and capacity prevent treating this comparison as an independently isolated connection intervention; the parent functions remain specified unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "R07-residue-unknowns",
      "source_refs": [
        "O6",
